// ============================================================================
// Project Poopdeck — Zero-Admin Power BI Semantic Model Extractor (Tier 2)
// ============================================================================
// Usage (Zero Fabric / Tenant Admin Rights Required):
//   1. Open the target report or semantic model in Power BI Desktop.
//   2. Switch to "DAX Query View" (left-hand rail in Power BI Desktop).
//   3. Run each EVALUATE block below (or run all 4 tabs) and click "Copy" ->
//      save as UTF-8 CSV or JSON into `vault/inbox/powerbi/<report_slug>/`:
//        - info_tables.csv        (from Query 1: INFO.TABLES())
//        - info_columns.csv       (from Query 2: INFO.COLUMNS())
//        - info_measures.csv      (from Query 3: INFO.MEASURES())
//        - info_relationships.csv (from Query 4: INFO.RELATIONSHIPS())
//   4. Run: `poopdeck sync powerbi --mode tier2`
//      Poopdeck extracts tables, columns, relationships, and DAX expressions,
//      redacts embedded credentials/PII, and flags heuristic / backward-looking
//      measures as BI-to-DS replacement candidates.
// ============================================================================

// Query 1 — Semantic Model Tables & Storage Modes
EVALUATE
INFO.TABLES()

// Query 2 — Table Columns, Data Types & Source Mappings
EVALUATE
INFO.COLUMNS()

// Query 3 — DAX Measures, Expressions & Descriptions
EVALUATE
INFO.MEASURES()

// Query 4 — Table Relationships, Cardinality & Cross-Filter Directions
EVALUATE
INFO.RELATIONSHIPS()
